  "abstract": {
    "value": "Controlling the reaction selectivity to achieve a precision synthesis is a constant concern for chemists. Here, we report a palladium-catalyzed deaminative coupling of propargylamines with arylboronic acids to generate allene skeletons. Importantly, this approach allows the regioselective γ-arylation of unactivated propargyl tertiary amines to access various allenes in the absence of amino-activating reagents. We present a wide range of propargylamines and boronic acids and demonstrate the synthetic application of the target products to ![](../extracted/assembly-of-diverse-allenes-via-activator-free-palladium-catalyzed-regioselective-arylation-of-propargylamines-with/images/6e26884088f83605b4b22c4bf30a271d99778dec8e49ba76552f7d6ece1c6431.jpg) <details> <summary>chemical</summary> Reaction scheme showing condensation of a pyrrolidine derivative with B(OH)2 under palladium catalyst to form a hydrogenated intermediate, with reagents and examples listed. </details>",
    "source": "markdown_inline_abstract",
